            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "One thing which is implemented separately in both which-key and mini.clue is the naming of keybind prefixes. which-key calls them groups and mini.clue calls them clues, but in both cases they consist of a set of modes, an input prefix, and a name. I can't find a ticket for it specifically, but this would also be useful for a command palette as it allows showing just the parent node of a tree of commands rather than the entire list of commands.\n\nHaving a built-in concept of command prefixes seems likely to be necessary to enable an ecosystem of \"out-of-the-box\" installable plugins that serve this need. I think this is especially important for capturing bindings created by other plugins which otherwise require additional manual configuration. Sometimes people use bindings to <Nop> to label groups, but I think that's probably going to cause some weirdness with input timeouts given https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/18877.\n\nI think that adding such groups would be a requirement for this feature, but could also be done without integrating some specific script that also handles things like showing options based on the current input state and command search.",
